{%- comment -%}
  LBASS HERO — MOBILE CORRECTIONS (2026-08-01)
  Rendered from snippets/lbass-hero-fx.liquid, which the section renders AFTER
  its own <style> block. Load order matters here: these rules deliberately sit
  last so they win ties without needing !important.

  TWO DEFECTS FOUND BY MEASURING A REAL 375px VIEWPORT, not by eye:

  1. TRUST BAR STAIRCASE. The mobile rule set overflow-x:auto to make the chips
     scroll in one row, but never reset flex-wrap. The desktop `flex-wrap:wrap`
     survived, so instead of scrolling the chips WRAPPED into three staggered
     rows (measured: chipRows 3, scrollWidth == clientWidth, so it never
     scrolled at all). overflow-x:auto does nothing while a flex row is still
     allowed to wrap — the two must be set together.

  2. SCARCITY LINE UNREADABLE. "ملي كتباع القطعة..." rendered #6B6B6E over the
     busiest part of the photograph, below the protected centre of the scrim.
     It is the one line carrying real scarcity, so it cannot be the least
     legible thing on the screen. Given the same plate treatment as the chips.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@media (max-width:767px){
  /* 2026-10-01: wrap, never clip. The row had flex-wrap:nowrap here (from the
     old one-line scroller) while lbass-hero-swap already set overflow-x:visible,
     so nothing scrolled and .lbh's overflow:hidden cut the last chip, COD, on
     every phone narrower than 390px: 3px at 375, 18px at 360, 58px at 320
     (measured). Tighter padding (and 11.5px text under 375px) keeps the four
     chips on one row from 360px up; narrower phones wrap instead of hiding COD. */
  .lbh .lbh-trust{ flex-wrap:wrap !important; gap:6px !important; }
  .lbh .lbh-ht{ padding:9px 10px; }

  .lbh .lbh-scarce{
    display:inline-block;
    margin-top:18px;
    padding:8px 12px;
    color:var(--fg);
    background:rgba(255,255,255,.86);
    border:1px solid var(--rule);
    backdrop-filter:blur(6px);
    line-height:1.5;
  }
  .lbh--ink .lbh-scarce{
    color:#F2F0EB;
    background:rgba(0,0,0,.52);
    border-color:rgba(242,240,235,.18);
  }
}
@media (max-width:374px){
  .lbh .lbh-ht{ padding:8px 8px; font-size:11.5px; }
}
</style>
